Package: patrone-guest-tools
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         linux-cloud-tools-generic-hwe-26.04 | linux-cloud-tools-generic,
         virtualbox-guest-utils,
         virtualbox-guest-x11
Description: PatroneOS's Hyper-V and VirtualBox guest support
 What a Windows guest gets from Hyper-V's integration services and
 VirtualBox's Guest Additions. Each part runs only under its own hypervisor
 (systemd's ConditionVirtualization), so a computer that isn't a virtual
 machine runs none of it.
 .
 On Hyper-V: shutdown from the host, heartbeat, time from the host (also
 as a source for chrony), key-value data exchange (the host sees the
 guest's name and IP addresses), VSS backup (production checkpoints) and
 the Guest Service Interface (Copy-VMFile from the host), from Ubuntu's
 kernel and its linux-cloud-tools daemons, with Patrone's own unit for file
 copy, which Ubuntu's no longer starts, and the daemons run from any
 installed kernel's tools. Dynamic memory needs nothing more.
 .
 On VirtualBox: Ubuntu's VirtualBox guest utilities (VBoxService for time
 sync, guest properties and shared folders; VBoxClient and VBoxDRMClient
 for the clipboard and resizing the screen with the window), started in
 Wayland sessions, which Ubuntu's packages don't do, and every account can
 use the shared folders. Those packages are in Ubuntu's multiverse
 section.
